"image": "/11909/11909_ms16800_1_14_010_thumb.jpg", "page": "14", "label": "10", "href": "/paper-summary/ordinance-14-november-1842/14"}, {"image": "/11909/11909_ms16800_1_14_011_thumb.jpg", "page": "15", "label": "11", "href": "/paper-summary/ordinance-14-november-1842/15"}, {"image": "/11909/11909_ms16800_1_14_012_thumb.jpg", "page": "16", "label": "12", "href": "/paper-summary/ordinance-14-november-1842/16"}, {"image": "/11909/11909_ms16800_1_14_013_thumb.jpg", "page": "17", "label": "13", "href": "/paper-summary/ordinance-14-november-1842/17"}, {"image": "/11909/11909_ms16800_1_14_014_thumb.jpg", "page": "18", "label": "14", "href": "/paper-summary/ordinance-14-november-1842/18"}, {"image": "/11909/11909_ms16800_1_14_015_thumb.jpg", "page": "19", "label": "15", "href": "/paper-summary/ordinance-14-november-1842/19"}, {"image": "/11909/11909_ms16800_1_14_016_thumb.jpg", "page": "20", "label": "16", "href": "/paper-summary/ordinance-14-november-1842/20"}, {"image": "/11909/11909_ms16800_1_14_017_thumb.jpg", "page": "21", "label": "17", "href": "/paper-summary/ordinance-14-november-1842/21"}, {"image": "/11909/11909_ms16800_1_14_018_thumb.jpg", "page": "22", "label": "18", "href": "/paper-summary/ordinance-14-november-1842/22"}, {"image": "/11909/11909_ms16800_1_14_019_thumb.jpg", "page": "23", "label": "[19]", "href": "/paper-summary/ordinance-14-november-1842/23"}, {"image": "/11909/11909_ms16800_1_14_020_thumb.jpg", "page": "24", "label": "[20]", "href": "/paper-summary/ordinance-14-november-1842/24"}], "tableOfContents": [], "summary": {"uri": "ordinance-14-november-1842", "series": "JSPPA", "urlTitleValue": "JSPPA6", "documentSeriesIdCompiled": "jsppa6-sub-nccr-sub02-421114", "documentSeriesUri": "/the-papers/administrative-records/jsppa6/jsppa6-sub-nccr/jsppa6-sub-nccr-sub02/jsppa6-sub-nccr-sub02-421114", "documentSeriesTitle": "<p>\r\n\tMeeting, 14 November 1842</p>", "editorialPageNumber": "17", "isPageNumberPresent": true, "searchUrl": "/published/jsp/searchable/papers/54016763/54016763-0021.xml", "clearText": "<html><head></head><body><div class=\"indent continuation wasptag\"> had issued at the time of the removal, transfer or concealment therein mentioned, if it be proven that the acts therein forbidden, were done with the intent to avoid the operation of such writ or Writs.</div> <div class=\"indent wasptag\">Section 13— Any Sheriff, or his Deputy, any Jailor or Coroner, having custody of any prisoner or prisoners<aside class=\"popup-wrapper\" id=\"17112318493980087472\"><a href=\"#17112318493980087472\" class=\"new-scribe-note staticPopup\" title=\"New Scribe\" name=\"trans23\"><img src=\"//cdn.churchofjesuschrist.org/ch/jsp/images/icn-new-scribe-16.png\" alt=\"Indicates a change in handwriting to a different scribe.\"></a><div class=\"popup-content\"><div class=\"note-data editorial-footnote\" isnote=\"Y\"><p class=\"bottom_0\">Insertion in the handwriting of first unidentified scribe.</p><hr></div></div></aside> committed on any Civil or Criminal, process, of any Court or Magistrate, who shall neglect to give such prisoner or prisoners<aside class=\"popup-wrapper\" id=\"16768264347771613470\"><a href=\"#16768264347771613470\" class=\"new-scribe-note staticPopup\" title=\"New Scribe\" name=\"trans24\"><img src=\"//cdn.churchofjesuschrist.org/ch/jsp/images/icn-new-scribe-16.png\" alt=\"Indicates a change in handwriting to a different scribe.\"></a><div class=\"popup-content\"><div class=\"note-data editorial-footnote\" isnote=\"Y\"><p class=\"bottom_0\">Insertion in the handwriting of first unidentified scribe.</p><hr></div></div></aside> a copy of the process, order or commitment by virtue of which he she or they are<aside class=\"popup-wrapper\" id=\"1003120881450532687\"><a href=\"#1003120881450532687\" class=\"new-scribe-note staticPopup\" title=\"New Scribe\" name=\"trans25\"><img src=\"//cdn.churchofjesuschrist.org/ch/jsp/images/icn-new-scribe-16.png\" alt=\"Indicates a change in handwriting to a different scribe.\"></a><div class=\"popup-content\"><div class=\"note-data editorial-footnote\" isnote=\"Y\"><p class=\"bottom_0\">Insertion in the handwriting of first unidentified scribe.</p><hr></div></div></aside> imprisoned, within six hours after demand made by said prisoner or prisoners<aside class=\"popup-wrapper\" id=\"11025757219241880225\"><a href=\"#11025757219241880225\" class=\"new-scribe-note staticPopup\" title=\"New Scribe\" name=\"trans26\"><img src=\"//cdn.churchofjesuschrist.org/ch/jsp/images/icn-new-scribe-16.png\" alt=\"Indicates a change in handwriting to a different scribe.\"></a><div class=\"popup-content\"><div class=\"note-data editorial-footnote\" isnote=\"Y\"><p class=\"bottom_0\">Insertion in the handwriting of first unidentified scribe.</p><hr></div></div></aside> or any one on his her or their<aside class=\"popup-wrapper\" id=\"18306202297100442581\"><a href=\"#18306202297100442581\" class=\"new-scribe-note staticPopup\" title=\"New Scribe\" name=\"trans27\"><img src=\"//cdn.churchofjesuschrist.org/ch/jsp/images/icn-new-scribe-16.png\" alt=\"Indicates a change in handwriting to a different scribe.\"></a><div class=\"popup-content\"><div class=\"note-data editorial-footnote\" isnote=\"Y\"><p class=\"bottom_0\">Insertion in the handwriting of first unidentified scribe.</p><hr></div></div></aside> behalf, shall forfeit five hundred Dollars<aside class=\"popup-wrapper\" id=\"12247251167868100431\"><a href=\"#12247251167868100431\" class=\"editorial-note-static staticPopup\" title=\"Note\" name=\"trans33\"><span id=\"documenttrans33\">33</span></a><div class=\"popup-content\"><div class=\"note-data editorial-footnote\" isnote=\"Y\"><p class=\"bottom_0\">Without such documentation, a prisoner could not apply for <a href=\"/topic/habeas-corpus\" class=\"referenceInPop\">habeas corpus</a>, as outlined in section 1.</p><hr></div></div></aside></div> <div class=\"indent wasptag\">Section 14— Any person who, knowing that another has been discharged by order of the Municipal Court, on a <aside class=\"popup-wrapper\" id=\"11070234763526992638\"><a href=\"#11070234763526992638\" class=\"reference staticPopup\" ro=\"x41899\" topic=\"x41899\" title=\"Habeas corpus\">Habeas Corpus</a><div class=\"popup-content\"><div class=\"note-data\" isnote=\"Y\" isnonsearchable=\"Y\"><input type=\"hidden\" value=\"Habeas corpus\"><p>“Have the body”; a written order from a court of competent jurisdiction commanding anyone having a person in custody to produce such person at a certain time and place and to state the reasons why he or she is being held in custody. The court will determine...</p><a class=\"more\" href=\"/topic/habeas-corpus\">View Glossary</a></div></div></aside> shall contrary to the provisions of this ordinance, arrest or detain him or her again for the same cause, which was shewn on [p. 17]</div></body></html>", "expandedText": "<html><head></head><body><div class=\"indent continuation wasptag\"> had issued at the time of the removal, transfer <span class=\"line-break\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span>or concealment therein mentioned, if it be proven <span class=\"line-break\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span>that the acts therein forbidden, were done with <span class=\"line-break\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span>the intent to avoid the operation of such writ &lt;​or Writs.​&gt;</div> <div class=\"indent wasptag\">Section 13— Any Sheriff, or his Deputy, any Jailor or <span class=\"line-break\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span>Coroner, having custody of any prisoner &lt;​or prisoners​&gt;<aside class=\"popup-wrapper\" id=\"18241701243120138946\"><a href=\"#18241701243120138946\" class=\"new-scribe-note staticPopup\" title=\"New Scribe\" name=\"trans23\"><img src=\"//cdn.churchofjesuschrist.org/ch/jsp/images/icn-new-scribe-16.png\" alt=\"Indicates a change in handwriting to a different scribe.\"></a><div class=\"popup-content\"><div class=\"note-data editorial-footnote\" isnote=\"Y\"><p class=\"bottom_0\">Insertion in the handwriting of first unidentified scribe.</p><hr></div></div></aside> committed <span class=\"line-break\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span>on any Civil or Criminal, process, of any Court or <span class=\"line-break\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span>Magistrate, who shall neglect to give such prisoner <span class=\"line-break\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span>&lt;​or prisoners​&gt;<aside class=\"popup-wrapper\" id=\"5020416014132051824\"><a href=\"#5020416014132051824\" class=\"new-scribe-note staticPopup\" title=\"New Scribe\" name=\"trans24\"><img src=\"//cdn.churchofjesuschrist.org/ch/jsp/images/icn-new-scribe-16.png\" alt=\"Indicates a change in handwriting to a different scribe.\"></a><div class=\"popup-content\"><div class=\"note-data editorial-footnote\" isnote=\"Y\"><p class=\"bottom_0\">Insertion in the handwriting of first unidentified scribe.</p><hr></div></div></aside> a copy of the process, order or commitment by <span class=\"line-break\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span>virtue of which he &lt;​&lt;​she​&gt; or they are​&gt;<aside class=\"popup-wrapper\" id=\"16985222585199515960\"><a href=\"#16985222585199515960\" class=\"new-scribe-note staticPopup\" title=\"New Scribe\" name=\"trans25\"><img src=\"//cdn.churchofjesuschrist.org/ch/jsp/images/icn-new-scribe-16.png\" alt=\"Indicates a change in handwriting to a different scribe.\"></a><div class=\"popup-content\"><div class=\"note-data editorial-footnote\" isnote=\"Y\"><p class=\"bottom_0\">Insertion in the handwriting of first unidentified scribe.</p><hr></div></div></aside> <span class=\"deleted\">is</span> imprisoned, within six hours <span class=\"line-break\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span>after demand made by said prisoner &lt;​or prisoners​&gt;<aside class=\"popup-wrapper\" id=\"16120046826269533439\"><a href=\"#16120046826269533439\" class=\"new-scribe-note staticPopup\" title=\"New Scribe\" name=\"trans26\"><img src=\"//cdn.churchofjesuschrist.org/ch/jsp/images/icn-new-scribe-16.png\" alt=\"Indicates a change in handwriting to a different scribe.\"></a><div class=\"popup-content\"><div class=\"note-data editorial-footnote\" isnote=\"Y\"><p class=\"bottom_0\">Insertion in the handwriting of first unidentified scribe.</p><hr></div></div></aside> or any one <span class=\"line-break\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span>on his &lt;​her or their​&gt;<aside class=\"popup-wrapper\" id=\"10995674598597541298\"><a href=\"#10995674598597541298\" class=\"new-scribe-note staticPopup\" title=\"New Scribe\" name=\"trans27\"><img src=\"//cdn.churchofjesuschrist.org/ch/jsp/images/icn-new-scribe-16.png\" alt=\"Indicates a change in handwriting to a different scribe.\"></a><div class=\"popup-content\"><div class=\"note-data editorial-footnote\" isnote=\"Y\"><p class=\"bottom_0\">Insertion in the handwriting of first unidentified scribe.</p><hr></div></div></aside> behalf, shall forfeit five hundred Dollars<aside class=\"popup-wrapper\" id=\"11701679976822489576\"><a href=\"#11701679976822489576\" class=\"editorial-note-static staticPopup\" title=\"Note\" name=\"trans33\"><span id=\"documenttrans33\">33</span></a><div class=\"popup-content\"><div class=\"note-data editorial-footnote\" isnote=\"Y\"><p class=\"bottom_0\">Without such documentation, a prisoner could not apply for <a href=\"/topic/habeas-corpus\" class=\"referenceInPop\">habeas corpus</a>, as outlined in section 1.</p><hr></div></div></aside></div> <div class=\"indent wasptag\">Section 14— Any person who, knowing that another <span class=\"line-break\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span>has been discharged by order of the Municipal <span class=\"line-break\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span>Court, on a <aside class=\"popup-wrapper\" id=\"1188617564648907349\"><a href=\"#1188617564648907349\" class=\"reference staticPopup\" ro=\"x41899\" topic=\"x41899\" title=\"Habeas corpus\">Habeas Corpus</a><div class=\"popup-content\"><div class=\"note-data\" isnote=\"Y\" isnonsearchable=\"Y\"><input type=\"hidden\" value=\"Habeas corpus\"><p>“Have the body”; a written order from a court of competent jurisdiction commanding anyone having a person in custody to produce such person at a certain time and place and to state the reasons why he or she is being held in custody. The court will determine...</p><a class=\"more\" href=\"/topic/habeas-corpus\">View Glossary</a></div></div></aside> shall contrary to the <span class=\"line-break\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span>provisions of this ordinance, arrest or detain him <span class=\"line-break\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span>&lt;​or her​&gt; again for the same cause, which was shewn on [p. 17]</div></body></html>", "calendarsOfDocuments": [], "versions": [{"versionTitle": "Ordinance, 14 November 1842", "versionLink": "/paper-summary/ordinance-14-november-1842/1", "versionFeatured": ""}, {"versionTitle": "Nauvoo City Council Minute Book, 1841–1845", "versionLink": "/paper-summary/nauvoo-city-council-minute-book-1841-1845/125", "versionFeatured": ""}, {"versionTitle": "Ordinance, 14 November 1842, as Published in the <em xmlns:tei=\"http://www.tei-c.org/ns/1.0\" xmlns:lds=\"https://ldsc.xmlref.com/local/ldschurch\">Wasp</em>", "versionLink": "/paper-summary/ordinance-14-november-1842-as-published-in-the-wasp/1", "versionFeatured": ""}, {"versionTitle": "History, 1838–1856, volume D-1 [1 August 1842–1 July 1843]", "versionLink": "/paper-summary/history-1838-1856-volume-d-1-1-august-1842-1-july-1843/58", "versionFeatured": ""}, {"versionTitle": "“History of Joseph Smith”", "versionLink": "/paper-summary/history-of-joseph-smith/451", "versionFeatured": ""}], "images": {"smallImageUrl": "/11909/11909_ms16800_1_14_017_thumb.jpg", "mediumImageUrl": "/11909/11909_ms16800_1_14_017_med.jpg", "largeImageUrl": "/11909/11909_ms16800_1_14_017.jpg", "downloadImageU